# SYNTHESISED to exercise the two provider-address shapes SIDE BY SIDE, so a
# filter can keep one and drop the other.
#
# terraform-plugin-sdk reports a bare "provider" for tf_provider_addr when a
# provider is served without a ProviderAddr in its ServeOpts (measured on
# terraform-provider-github v6.3.1 across 1,104 lines of a real HCP log), and
# internal/span substitutes the component name in its place -- so one of this
# log's RPC providers is "provider.terraform-provider-github_v6.3.1", which
# has no "/" and so no derivable provider type. The other,
# "registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/local", is in registry form and its type
# derives from its last segment.
#
# Two are needed because the facet pane starts with every value TICKED:
# leaving one address in the allow-list means unticking the other, so a log
# with a single provider cannot express "narrowed to this address" at all.
# The pair also puts the two rules against each other on one fixture -- keep
# the registry address and the UI tier narrows with it, keep the bare one and
# the UI tier is left alone (see uiProviderTypes).
#
# It carries UI-hook spans under two DIFFERENT implied providers (github and
# local) so that a rule deriving a type from the bare address anyway would be
# visible: no UI provider can equal any segment of it, so both rows' figures
# would go to zero at once.
#
# The hclog lines follow testdata/provider-rpc.log's "Received downstream
# response" shape; the terraform.ui JSON lines follow
# testdata/two-tier.log's apply_start/apply_complete shape. Values are
# invented; no line here is from a real run.
